Manual review corrections, verified against the live OpenStax page (upstream
oddities such as "0<z<=1" on the cube surface, the self-cancelling
x^2+y^2-x^2 term, and "orientated" for "oriented" were all confirmed to be
faithful transcriptions of the source text and left untouched):

- Item 3 (line 20): the math span closed one character too late, trapping
  the following semicolon and "S" inside math mode ($...\mathbf{k};S$ is...)
  instead of the ";" S is..." pattern used by every sibling item in this
  file. Moved the closing $ to immediately after \mathbf{k}.
- Item 8 (line 25): the parenthetical "(constant a>0)" was split so that
  "(constant" rendered in \text{} (upright) while "a>0)" fell back to raw
  math mode (italic), producing inconsistent fonts across one phrase and a
  stray closing paren left in math mode. Rewrapped as
  \text{ (constant }a>0\text{)} so the parentheses and word "constant" are
  upright text and only the variable expression is math italic.
- Item near line 52 (radial field between spheres of radius 1 and 2): the
  norm was written with raw ASCII double pipes (||\mathbf{r}||) instead of
  the \|...\| delimiter macro; normalized to \|\mathbf{r}\|, matching the
  \|\mathbf{R}\| notation already used for the same kind of norm elsewhere
  in this file.

